## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-aware tracing in serverless multi-tenant workflows with per-tenant sampling. Emphasizes deterministic sampling, fault isolation, and fidelity under bursts.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health propagation across hops
- per-tenant sampling policies
- deterministic sampling using traceId hashing
- serverless orchestration and edge aggregation
- fidelity during micro-bursts

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldSample(tenantId, traceId, health, rates) {
  const rate = rates[tenantId] ?? 0;
  const seed = hashCode(traceId + '|' + tenantId);
  return (Math.abs(seed) % 1000) < rate * 1000;
}
function hashCode(s){
  let h=0; for(let i=0;i<s.length;i++){ h=(h*31 + s.charCodeAt(i))|0; } return h;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you simulate degradation and verify sampling fairness across tenants?
- How would you integrate with existing tracing backends and ensure tail-latency guarantees?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-driven incentives in streaming, including how CKNE affects throughput, partitioning, and latency, plus a stable rebalancing loop and end-to-end validation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-throughput/partition mapping
- Kafka partition rebalancing and windowing impact
- Baseline SLA guarantees with dynamic prioritization
- Telemetry, monitoring, and stability guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-mapping for CKNE-driven resource allocation
function mapCKNETokens(ckne, baseThroughput, basePartitions, kappa, lambda, minP, maxP){
  const T = baseThroughput * (1 + kappa * (ckne - 0.5));
  const P = Math.max(minP, Math.min(maxP, Math.round(basePartitions * (1 + lambda * (ckne - 0.5)))));
  return {throughput: T, partitions: P};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical implementation of CKNE-driven throughput control at the API gateway layer, specifically assessing the ability to translate abstract CKNE values into concrete resource quotas and deadlines, and to adapt these allocations in real-time based on performance metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic CKNE-to-resource quota mapping
- Token bucket algorithm with CKNE-weighted refill rates
- Real-time rebalancing loop with SLA preservation
- Fairness constraints while prioritizing high-value tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: CKNE-driven resource rebalancing executed minute-by-minute
function rebalanceResources(tenants) {
  tenants.forEach(tenant => {
    // Scale token refill rate by CKNE value
    tenant.tokens += baseRefillRate * tenant.ckne;

    // Adjust upstream deadline inversely with CKNE
    tenant.deadline = baseDeadline / (tenant.ckne + 1);

    // Enforce maximum allocation caps
    tenant.tokens = Math.min(tenant.tokens, maxTokenCap);
  });
}
```

## Implementation Strategy

The system continuously monitors per-tenant performance metrics and reallocates resources toward higher-CKNE tenants while maintaining baseline p95 latency guarantees through a controlled feedback loop that preserves fairness across the tenant population.
